rif;font-size:12px;font-weight:100;line-height:18px\"><p class=\"date\" style=\"font-style:italic;color:#8b8b8b;font-weight:400\">September 27, 2026</p></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table><table><tbody><tr><td style=\"padding:28px 20px 4px 20px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:20px;color:#757575\"></td></tr></tbody></table><table class=\"body-copy\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;border:0px;word-break:break-word\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"padding:12px 20px 12px 20px;font-size:13px;line-height:20px;color:#333333;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><div style=\"margin:0;padding:15px 0px 0px 0px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd\"></div><table class=\"whats-changed\" style=\"table-layout:fixed;margin-right:20px;margin-bottom:18px;width:100%\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12px;font-weight:600;line-height:18px;color:#6775b8;width:120px;border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd\">WHAT'S CHANGED?</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:20px;padding:4px 0px 0px 0px;color:#333333;font-weight:600;width:100%;text-align:left\">Applied Materials Inc. (AMAT.O)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12px;color:#333333;font-weight:400;line-height:20px;padding:0px 0px 0px 0px\">Price Target</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd\"><table style=\"table-layout:fixed;width:100%\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:20px;color:#333333;padding:0px 0px 4px 0px\">From:   $642.00</td><td style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:20px;color:#333333;padding:0px 0px 4px 0px;text-align:left\">To: <strong>$563.00</strong></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table><table style=\"table-layout:fixed;width:100%\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"padding:0px 0px 14px 0px;width:100%;table-layout:fixed;width:100%\"><table style=\"table-layout:fixed;width:100%\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"width:100%;padding:0px 0px 8px 0px;width:100%;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:24px;color:#333333;font-weight:400;border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd\"><table><tbody><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 0px 0px 0px;vertical-align:top;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:24px;color:#333333;font-weight:400\"><div>SEMICON has been a positive catalyst for SPE more often than not (absolute), but not relative (vs SOX). </div></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table><table style=\"table-layout:fixed;width:100%\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"width:100%;table-layout:fixed;width:100%;padding-bottom:12px;padding-top:6px\"><table class=\"body-copy\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;border:0px;word-break:break-word\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"keyTakaway_wrapper\" style=\"color:#333333;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><div class=\"keyTakeaways\"><table><tbody><tr><td class=\"single_takeaway\" style=\"font-size:13px;line-height:20px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Key takeaway: Expect lots of positive commentary (to no surprise) and themes similar to SEMICON Taiwan and ECOC. </td></tr></tbody></table></div></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table><div class=\"MS_synopsis\"><p>What we’ll hear from the conference. We think the key topics will be very similar to <a href=\"https://ny.matrix.ms.com/eqr/article/webapp/068b3268-a842-11f1-994b-8660e17eee51?ch=rp&amp;sch=sr&amp;sr=5\" target=\"_blank\">SEMICON Taiwan </a>and <a href=\"https://ny.matrix.ms.com/eqr/article/webapp/86e89e36-b66c-11f1-a440-99a719172027?ch=rp&amp;sch=ar\" target=\"_blank\">ECOC</a>, with significant commentary around silicon photonics and related testing, advanced packaging, and, to a lesser extent, memory optimization. These themes have been top of mind throughout the year, and we expect the takeaways to be evolutionary rather than revolutionary. What we’ll hear from the companies. Not surprisingly, we expect company messaging at SEMICON to come in various forms of: “demand is strengthening,” “visibility is extending,” “supply chain cooperation is closer than ever,” and “we’re building out capacity.” We see this as more of a reiteration of existing trends than anything meaningfully new. One theme we’re increasingly focused on, but are unlikely to get much color on, is whether WFE is becoming more of a volume market or remains primarily a technology market, as customers add greenfield capacity for N-1 nodes while pockets of the technology roadmap face delays.</p><p>Company events: 2 coverage companies are hosting larger events for the financial community. 1) AMAT Investor Breakfast: Unlike the past 3 years, when AMAT hosted a “Technology Breakfast,” the company is hosting an “Investor Breakfast” on the 13th. Our understanding is that the event will fall somewhere between a Technology Breakfast and a traditional Investor Day. We do not expect a point-specific model to be presented, but anticipate the company will provide some financial indicators. 2) CAMT Breakfast: for more details see <a href=\"https://ny.matrix.ms.com/eqr/article/webapp/17b7bd4e-b8f1-11f1-a440-99a719172027\" target=\"_blank\">4 Qs into SEMICON West</a>.</p><p>Trading SEMICON. Over the last 10 shows, SEMICON has been a positive catalyst for SPE, with the group posting an average return of 4.1% over the two weeks leading into and one week following the show, and positive returns around 7 of the last 10 events. Returns have been stronger during upcycles (+5.7%) than downcycles (+2.6%). Relative to the SOX, however, performance has been more subdued, with returns roughly flat. Thoughts on AMAT. We fine-tune our CY27 revenue/EPS forecasts for AMAT from $50.2bn/$20.44 to $50.7bn/$20.92 as we raise our NAND and GM% forecasts. We lower our target multiple from 26x to 22x, with 22x representing a ~10% premium to the company’s 20x through-cycle average since 2020. We believe SPE multiples track most closely with GM%, and we model meaningful margin expansion for AMAT this upcycle (CY25 48.8%, CY27 52.0%). The market is giving AMAT the benefit of the doubt, and we agree with that assessment; however, we prefer names where expectations are less reflected in the multiple. Remain EW. <a href=\"https://ny.matrix.ms.com/eqr/article/webapp/19f2e57a-b1df-11f1-b79c-85eb549cca22?t=1790544449:221:1648850:95722cac585c&amp;m=1&amp;ch=CDF Research ISG#e=ZmVsaXBlLm1vbnRlaXJvQGNhcHN0b25lLmNvbS5icg==\" style=\"font-weight:600;color:#2a9cd6\">Read more...</a></p></div><table><tbody><tr><td style=\"padding:4px 0px 10px 0px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:24px;color:#757575\"></td></tr></tbody></table><table style=\"float:none;clear:both\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:28px;padding:12px 0px 16px 0px;color:#333333;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:600\">Authors</td></tr></tbody></table><table class=\"authors\" style=\"width:280px;border-collapse:collapse;table-layout:fixed;clear:both\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"padding:0px 0px 18px 0px;border-right:20px solid #fff\"></td><td style=\"padding:0px 6px 18px 0px\"><p style=\"font-size:9px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-weight:100;color:#696969;text-transform:uppercase\">Morgan Stanley &amp; Co. LLC</p><p style=\"padding:6px 0px 6px 0px;font-size:13px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-weight:600;color:#333333\">Shane Brett</p><p style=\"font-size:11px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-weight:400\">+1 212 761-1022       <a href=\"mailto:Shane.Brett@morganstanley.com?subject=Re:IDEA%3A%20Semiconductor%20Capital%20Equipment%3A%20SEMICON%20West%20Preview\" style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-weight:100;color:#696969;border:1px solid #ededed;padding:4px 4px 2px 4px;text-decoration:none;font-size:9px\">EMAIL </a></p></td></tr></tbody></table><